Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_RING_GIVERS_PEDIA	The Ring-givers' faith is practiced through artifice. Each accomplishment or blessing is added to their collection of charms, rings and baubles. Nantosuelta is known as the Queen of Bells (by those who build temples to her), Keymaker (by the tinkerers who practice the most intricate and arcane of her artifice) and the Mother of Knights (by warriors that rely only on their skills, weapon and her charms to protect themselves)\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t[PARAGRAPH:2]State religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_MITHRIL_GOLEM]The Mithril Golem[\\LINK] (world unit and summon)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_PRIEST_RINGGIVER]Artificer [\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_HIGH_PRIEST_RINGGIVER]Instructor [\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_TANK]Tank [\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Halves the production cost of: [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_GUILD_OF_HAMMERS]The Guild of Endeavors[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_SCULPTORS_STUDIO]Scultors' Studio[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_ADULARIA_CHAMBER]Adularia Chamber[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_BLASTING_WORKSHOP]Blasting Workshop[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_GOLEM_TRACKS]Golem Tracks[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_PALLENS_ENGINE]Pallens Engine[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_FORM_OF_THE_TITAN]Form of the Titan[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_PALACE_LUCHUIRP]The Luchuirp Palace[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:2]Units of this faith are more likely to gain affinity for [LINK=BONUS_MANA_ENCHANTMENT]Enchantment[\\LINK] mana\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], The [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Good lands and weakened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_ENCHANTMENT]Enchantment Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CLOCKWORK_CITY]Clockwork City[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WORKSHOP]Workshops[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CITADEL]Citadels[\\LINK], or [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_DIMENSIONAL]Dimensional Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_TAPESTRY_HOUSE]Tapestry House[\\LINK], and [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_PORTAL]Portals[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n\t\t	
