Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL_PEDIA	Arawn pays no attention to creation, occupying himself with the matters of the afterworld instead. Despite this some few choose to worship him, though it is as useful as worshiping a rock. Often called the Unhearing God because he ignores his worshipers.\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], and The [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK]. It will be weakened in Good or Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_DEATH]Death Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_YGGDRASIL]Yggdrasil[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_BRADELINES_WELL]Bradeline's Well[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_GRAVEYARD]Graveyards[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_BROKEN_SEPULCHUR]the Broken Sepulchur[\\LINK], or [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_LIFE]Life Mana[\\LINK].\r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL	Grey Council	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL_ADJECTIVE	Adjudicator	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL_PEDIA	Judges sought out to adjudicate between different parties. Their religion preaches against bias and imparts decisions without local or personal influence. Mechanic: The Grey Council is a voting body where the player can participate in elections with other players. Often called the Adjudicator.\r\n\r\n\r\n[PARAGRAPH][ICON_BULLET]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK] will have its arda strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Neutral lands and weakened in Good or Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_FORCE]Force Mana[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_SEVEN_PINES]the Seven Pines[\\LINK], or [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_RING_OF_WARDING]Rings of Warding[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n\t\t	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION	Ember Legionnaire	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION_PEDIA	The church of Bhall has little long-lasting structure. Instead religious upheavals happen and huge masses of fanatical followers rise up and rebel against whatever is being protested in that area. The cause is less important than the fervor, the blessing of Bhall, and the violence that comes with the rebellion. Most worshipers of Bhall receive a brand of her mark that forever burns and inflicts pain. Bhall is also known as the Queen of Fire and the Fallen Star.\r\n\r\n\r\n[PARAGRAPH][ICON_BULLET]Priests and Demons of  [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK]. It will be weakened in Neutral and strengthened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_FIRE]Fire Mana[\\LINK] and weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_WATER]Water Mana[\\LINK]. It is strenthened near the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_PYRE_OF_THE_SERAPHIC]Pyre of the Seraphic[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_HELLFIRE]Hellfire[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_PIT]Pits of Torment[\\LINK], [LINK=TERRAIN_BURNING_SANDS]Burning Sands[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_SMOKE]Smoke[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_FLAMES]Flames[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_FOREST_BURNT]Burnt Forests[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_JUNGLE]Jungles[\\LINK], and [LINK=FEATURE_TORMENTED_SOULS]Tormented Souls[\\LINK], and weakened on [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n\t\t	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD	Sons of Discord	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD_ADJECTIVE	Son of Discord	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD_PEDIA	The church of Camulos wants war between all nations. He is known as the Sanguine Fountain and the Hundred Armed God. On the nights before large battles, the skies echo with the shrill cries of Camulos's demons, peering out expectantly for the coming war. In cities that don't outlaw them, temples to Camulos are brutal arenas where corpses of the freshly killed lie in piles, feral animals feast on the bodies, and nearly every stone is blood stained. This is a religion based on hate. It is racist in some countries, anti-cultural group in others. The target doesn't matter to the religion, only the hate that is fueled by it. \r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Demons of [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], Undertow, [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK]. It will be weakened in Good or neutral lands and strengthened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_CHAOS]Chaos Mana[\\LINK] and weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_LAW]Law Mana[\\LINK]. It is strenthened on Wastelands, Fields of Perdition, [LINK=FEATURE_BLIZZARD]Blizzards[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_TORMENTED_SOULS]Tormented Souls[\\LINK], and weakened on [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_ORDER_PEDIA	[TAB]Junil, the elder of the Gods, had promised to stay apart from the conflict in Creation. While other gods pressed the limits of the Compact or blatantly ignored it, he held to its restrictions and spirit. Even when his church was a mockery of his dominion, he would not respond. It was only when the compact was openly broken, when fallen angels walked in creation that he responded to help the least of men. He asked only one thing in return: unquestioning obedience. [PARAGRAPH:2]The Order was founded during the Age of Magic, not from divine inspiration but from the growing requirements of the Patrian bureaucracy. The codex of Patrian law had become so byzantine and severe that nearly autonomous inquisitors were needed to carry out it requirements. These inquisitors were magically bound to the codex so that they wouldn't become corrupted by their station. They drew upon the name of Junil, God of Law, in taking their oaths and in carrying out their brutal decrees. [PARAGRAPH:1]These inquisitors were feared nearly as much as Kylorin's Archmages and would come to a city to adjudicate major disputes and to see that justice, as defined by the codex of Patria, was followed. [PARAGRAPH:1]At the head of the church was Soqed Hozi. It is said that if she spoke a lie, reality would change to make it into truth. Soqed had a mute twin who was little more than a dim shadow of her powerful sister. The two remained at the Temple of Atonement where they oversaw the church and its inquisitors. [PARAGRAPH:1]The ideology of Junil was secondary to the church's task of maintaining the laws of Patria. Some lesser confessors began to question: "What was the use of following the law if it was corrupt?". The most conflicted of these was Sphener, an inquisitor who killed demons in his service to the church. He had gazed into hell and it was only his strict adherence to his faith that allowed him to survive. Sphener obeyed every edict of the church, but argued that worship of Junil was the greatest mission of the church. [PARAGRAPH:1]The church found out about the whispered concerns of some of its members and launched the Purge of Whispers, and attempt to execute anyone in the church who questioned church doctrine. [PARAGRAPH:1]The purge was horribly effective and killed members of the church, family and friends. It covered many cities over all of Patria and happened in a single night. Sphener was one of the few that escaped the purge and the next day the church held a trial for him in absentia. They convicted him and sentenced him to death upon the wheel. Condemned by his law, his church, and his god, Sphener came to the church on his own and accepted his execution. He was broken as the church elders and the public watched. [PARAGRAPH:1]Over the next decade Sphener's spirit was seen hundreds of times tending to those in need. He tended to those unfairly persecuted by the church and ministered to church members that prayed to Junil for guidance. This became the basis for the new Order church that would be founded in the Age of Rebirth. [PARAGRAPH:3]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_TEMPLE_OF_THE_ORDER]Basilica[\\LINK] (building)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=BUILDING_LORUM_DIABOLI]Lorum Diaboli[\\LINK] (world wonder)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_PRIEST_OF_THE_ORDER]Confessor[\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_HIGH_PRIEST_OF_THE_ORDER]Prior[\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_Pontiff]Pontiff[\\LINK] ([LINK=CIVILIZATION_BANNOR]Bannor[\\LINK] unique unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_CRUSADER]Crusader[\\LINK] (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_VALIN]Valin Phanuel[\\LINK] (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_SPHENER]Sphener[\\LINK] (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=CIVIC_SOCIAL_ORDER]Social Order[\\LINK] (civic)[PARAGRAPH:2]The Order has major conflicts with both The Ashen Veil and The Undertow. One may prevent the spread of another into a city, or drive the other out.\r\n\r\n\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], amd the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Good lands and weakened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_LAW]Law Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_TEMPLE_OF_ATONEMENT]Temple of Atonement[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CITADEL]Citadels[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CASTLE]Castles[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_FORT]Forts[\\LINK], or [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_CHAOS]Chaos Mana[\\LINK] and [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CARNIVEANS_CRAG]Carnivean's Craig[\\LINK].\r\n\t\t	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN_PEDIA	[TAB]Where the Order values law, the Empyrean values wisdom. Adjudication started from the teachings of Lugus and punishment is not based on adherence to a labyrinthine codex of laws, but from direct consultation on the merits of each case. Social equality and impartiality are the model between a government and its citizens as well as between empires. As such the Empyrean gives equal voice to small empires as it does those that dominate Erebus. [PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Radiant Guard (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Ratha (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Vicar (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Chalid Astrakein (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CITADEL_OF_LIGHT]Citadel of Light[\\LINK] (improvement)[PARAGRAPH:2]The Empyrean has major conflicts with both The Ashen Veil and the Council of Esus. One may prevent the spread of another into a city, or drive the other out. [PARAGRAPH:2]The Empyrean was the driving force behind the founding of the Overcouncil. No player may adopt the Overcouncil civic until this religion is founded. [PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Good lands and weakened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_SUN]Sun Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_MIRROR_OF_HEAVEN]Mirror of Heaven[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_SPIRE_OF_THE_SUN]Spire of the Sun[\\LINK], a [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CITADEL_OF_LIGHT]Citadel of Light[\\LINK], a [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_TOWER]Tower[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK], or [LINK=TERRAIN_DESERT]Desert[\\LINK] terrain. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_SHADOW]Shadow Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WHISPERING_WOOD]Whispering Wood[\\LINK], or [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WODES_OAK]Wode's Oak[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_RUNES_PEDIA	[TAB]Kilmorph is the goddess of the earth, She Who Dwells Beneath. She formed children out of stone, the Dwarves, and taught them the secrets of metalworking. One of the first religions available to the men of the world, Kilmorph will answer the prayers of honorable men and even send her soldiers to defend their cities. [PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Soldier of Kilmorph (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Paramander (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Stonewarden (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Bambur (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Arete (civic)[PARAGRAPH:1]Building Mines and Quarries on Peaks\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH][ICON_BULLET]A priest of the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK] will have its arda most strengthened by the influence of the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Good or Neutral lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_EARTH]Earth Mana[\\LINK], Peaks, Hills, the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_STANDING_STONES]Standing Stones[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_MINE]Mines[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_QUARRY]Quarries[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_FORT]Forts[\\LINK], or [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_AIR]Air Mana[\\LINK], flatlands, rivers, Flood Plains, and water. It is stronger the longer the unit has been fortifying in place. \r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_LEAVES_PEDIA	[TAB]Deep in the woods, the whispers of Elves linger. Ancient protectors normally above the affairs of men, some men have shown enough loyalty to them to be taught their magic and even gain the assistance of the Satyrs. [PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_FAWN]Fawn (unit)[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB][LINK=UNIT_SATYR]Satyr (unit)[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Priest of Leaves (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Yvain (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Kithra Kyriel (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Guardian of Nature (civic)[PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion blocks access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Removing[LINK=FEATURE_FOREST] Forest[\\LINK] [PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Building [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_LUMBERMILL]Lumbermills[\\LINK] [NEWLINE][NEWLINE]While the Fellowship of Leaves is your state religion every forest in your empire has a 3% chance per turn of upgrading to an [LINK=FEATURE_ANCIENT_FOREST]ancient forest[\\LINK]. \r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], and the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened in Neutral lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_NATURE]Nature Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_YGGDRASIL]Yggdrasil[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_TOMB_OF_SUCELLUS]Tomb of Sucellus[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_HERVES_MAUSOLEUM]Herve's Mausoleum[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CAMP]Camps[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_FOREST_ANCIENT]Ancient Forests[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_FOREST]Forests[\\LINK], [LINK=FEATURE_FOREST_NEW]New Forests[\\LINK], or [LINK=FEATURE_FOREST_BURNT]Burnt Forests[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_ICE]Ice Mana[\\LINK].	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS	Undertow	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_OVERLORDS_PEDIA	[TAB]The power beneath the Aegean waves is said to be more powerful than any other, but the Undertow are unfocused and follow a thousand different obscure agendas. The Disciples of the Undertow dare not expose themselves directly to the conflicting commands of their masters and instead use the poor as intermediaries. They are quickly driven insane by the process, which the disciples prefer as it keeps them from manipulating the message. They also share the process of turning a warrior into The Drown, undead thralls, a process with few volunteers. [PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Asylum (building)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]unlimited Cultists (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Stygian Guard (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]The Drown (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Saverous (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Hemah (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:2]The cult of the Undertow has major conflicts with The Order. One may prevent the spread of another into a city, or drive the other out.\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_LAERAN_CORD]The Laeran Cord[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK]. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_WATER]Water Mana[\\LINK], [LINK=BONUS_MANA_MIND]Mind Mana[\\LINK], [LINK=BONUS_JETEYE]Jeteye[\\LINK], Water Terrain, Rivers, Flood Plains, the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_AIFON_ISLE]Aifon Isle[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_FISHING_BOATS]Fishing Boats[\\LINK], or [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WHALING_BOATS]Whaling Boats[\\LINK]. It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_FIRE]Fire Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_RING_OF_CARCER]Ring of Carcer[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_PYRE_OF_THE_SERAPHIC]Pyre of the Seraphic[\\LINK], Peaks, and Hills.\r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS_PEDIA	[TAB]A secret council that is so good at spreading lies that it is often unaware of the truth of its own stories. They have "thrones" (secret meeting places) in most major cities and excel at sneaking goods and people into or out of areas. Esus is known as the King of Thieves, Jack Shadow, and Moonsong, though it's popular for religious leaders to take these names for themselves as well. [PARAGRAPH:2]Founding[PARAGRAPH]This is the most common legend spread about the founding of the religion. No one knows if it's actually true. [PARAGRAPH]Unknown to the other gods, Esus slips into creation from time to time. Most commonly as a traveling minstrel (male or female as it suits him), but occasionally as a merchant, beggar, jackal or crow. [PARAGRAPH]On one of these trips he met Oriol Peregrinus, a priest of Kilmorph who had been stealing from his temple for years. The night before he was to go face trial he sat in a bar drinking and whispering prayers to any god that would hear him, as his own certainly wouldn't forgive his crime. [PARAGRAPH]Esus, who was playing at the bar, overheard him and went to comfort the man. The two shared drinks and eventually Oriol shared his story. Esus offered a lie that Oriol could tell to the church, but Oriol was still worried that he wouldn't be believed. At that Esus offered him an opal scarab that would make anyone believe his lies. [PARAGRAPH]Oriol took the scarab and went to his trial before the church elders. To his surprise, they believed his lies without question. Those that accused him were punished and it increased his standing in the church of Kilmorph. [PARAGRAPH]A year later Esus returned and found Oriol at the bar again. This time he was ruined, he barely had the money to pay for his drink and had lost everything in the world that mattered to him. Esus asked what was wrong and he said that no one believed anything he said. He thought the scarab was cursed and threw it away. [PARAGRAPH]Esus explained that he had made the man's lies believable, but at a cost that no one would believe anything Oriol said that was true. If Oriol told his wife he loved her, she wouldn't believe him. [PARAGRAPH]Oriol sobbed into his drink. [PARAGRAPH]"What is your name?" Esus asked. [PARAGRAPH]"Oriol. " Oriol said, still staring into his drink. [PARAGRAPH]"I don't believe you. " Esus said. "I think your name is Mendax Opacous. "[PARAGRAPH]"My name is Mendax?" Oriol asked. [PARAGRAPH]"That sounds better. That is a name people will believe. " Esus said. "And what god do you worship? Surely not Kilmorph, I think you worship Esus, the god of shadows. "[PARAGRAPH]"I worship the god of shadows?" Oriol asked. [PARAGRAPH]"Yes you do. See how easy this is. " Esus said. "And remember that you can tell any woman you love her, and she will believe you. As long as it isn't true. If you actually love her then your words will be sour to her ears, your affections will poison her against you. You can go to a new city, start a new life, raise up a church to Esus, as long as you know that it is all pretend. "[PARAGRAPH]"I have already lost my wife's love to your curse. " Oriol said. "I have lost my standing in the church, you should have me abandon my faith as well? What if I just go to church elders and tell them about what you have done to me?"[PARAGRAPH]"You could try, but who would believe you?" Esus said with a smile. [PARAGRAPH]Oriol, now going by Mendax, did as Esus suggested and founded the first Aphotic Throne in an abandoned Patrian manor (it was easy enough to convince them that he was the real owner). The traditions of that throne were largely made up by him in a tangled weave of whatever inspiration struck him in the moment. It was said that his biggest secret was that he kept a small shrine of Kilmorph until the day he died. [PARAGRAPH:3]Sects[PARAGRAPH]Every Throne could be considered its own sect. There is no common communication, rules or traditions between them. Some are brutal and vengeful, others are lighthearted and free. They tend to be the opposite of the communities they exist in. Sometimes they are the secret power behind the city government, and sometimes they are teenage adventurers pretending at being a secret organization. [PARAGRAPH:3]An oddity among the religions, the Council of Esus has no temples or ordinary disciples. As a secret society, it cannot be [LINK=SPELL_EVANGELIZE]Evangelized[\\LINK] openly to either cities or all the units nearby. However, any unit which is a member can pay to establish a local Council presence in any city. Units without another State Religion prerequisite, and with a leader with the right State Religion, can spend gold to purchase an initiation from an Esus [LINK=PROMOTION_EVANGELIZE]Evangelist[\\LINK] on the same plot. That theme, paying for miracles, is common in the Council of Esus. [PARAGRAPH]Esus's priests have the abilities of Spies, including the ability to steal plans, destroy city production, and sabotage improvements including even Unique Features. [PARAGRAPH]State Religion allows access to the [LINK=UNIT_SHADOWRIDER]Shadowrider[\\LINK], [LINK=UNIT_DISCIPLE_ESUS]Swindler [\\LINK], [LINK=UNIT_PRIEST_ESUS]Thief[\\LINK], and [LINK=UNIT_HIGH_PRIEST_ESUS]Propogandist[\\LINK] units. [PARAGRAPH]The Council of Esus has major conflicts with The Empyrean. One may prevent the spread of another into a city, or drive the other out. [PARAGRAPH]The Council of Esus was the driving force behind the founding of the Undercouncil in opposition to the Overcouncil. No player may adopt the Undercouncil civic until this religion is founded, nor may any player with this state religion join the Overcouncil. \r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH:3]Priests and Angels of [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK]. It will be weakened in Good lands, strengthened in Neutral or Evil lands.It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_SHADOW]Shadow Mana[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WODES_OAK]Wode's Oak[\\LINK], and the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_WHISPERING_WOOD]Whispering Wood[\\LINK], It is weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_SUN]Sun Mana[\\LINK], the [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_MIRROR_OF_HEAVEN]Mirror of Heaven[\\LINK], and [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_CITADEL_OF_LIGHT]Citadels of Light[\\LINK]. 	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_ASHEN_PEDIA	[TAB]Mages spent weeks in meditation, exploring the farthest reaches of the ethereal world. The demands of the body were ignored, and they survived sustained only by magic. Their efforts were rewarded, a sentience was contacted, dark and horrible. It whispered secrets into the mages' minds, secrets of necromancy, diseases, and sacrificial rites. It promised power in exchange for their blood, and they freely gave it. [PARAGRAPH:2]State Religion allows access to:[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Demons' Altar (building)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Diseased Corpse (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Ritualist (unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Rosier the Fallen (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Mardero (world unit)[PARAGRAPH:1][TAB]Sacrifice the Weak (civic)[PARAGRAPH:2]The Ashen Veil has major conflicts with both The Order and The Empyrean. One may prevent the spread of another into a city, or drive the other out. \r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n[PARAGRAPH][ICON_BULLET]Priests and Demons of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK] will have their ardas most strengthened by the influence of [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], but also strengthened to a lesser degree by [LINK=RELIGION_COVEN]The Between[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_EMBER_LEGION]The Ember Legion[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ANOINTED]The Anointed[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_STEWARDS_OF_INEQUITY]The Stewards of Inequity[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_WHITE_HAND]The White Hand[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_COUNCIL_OF_ESUS]The Council of Esus[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_OCTOPUS_OVERLORDS]The Undertow[\\LINK]. Its arda will be weakened by [LINK=RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE]The Children of The One[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_MATRONAE]The Matronae[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Order[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_THE_EMPYREAN]The Empyrean[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_UNBLEMISHED]The Unblemished[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_RINGGIVER]The Ringgivers[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_BROTHERHOOD_OF_WARDENS]The Brotherhood of Wardens[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_GREY_COUNCIL]The Grey Council[\\LINK], the [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_ETERNAL_CABAL]The Eternal Cabal[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_CULT_OF_THE_DRAGON]Cult of the Dragon[\\LINK], [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK], and [LINK=RELIGION_FELLOWSHIP_OF_LEAVES]The Fellowship of the Leaves[\\LINK]. It will be weakened in Good and strengthened in Evil lands. It will be strengthened by proximity to [LINK=BONUS_MANA_ENTROPY]Entropy Mana[\\LINK] and weakened by [LINK=BONUS_MANA_CREATION]Creation Mana[\\LINK]. It is strenthened near [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_GRAVE_OF_ASMODAY]the Grave of Asmoday[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_HELLFIRE]Hellfire[\\LINK], [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_PIT]Pits of Torment[\\LINK], and [LINK=FEATURE_TORMENTED_SOULS]Tormented Souls[\\LINK], and weakened on [LINK=FEATURE_HALLOWED_GROUND]Hallowed Ground[\\LINK]. \r\n\r\n	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_WHITE_HAND	The White Hand	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_RELIGION_CHILDREN_OF_THE_ONE	Children of The One	
